.TH OPEN-MEDIA-CONVERTER 1 "September 2026" "Open Media Converter" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
open-media-converter \- convert media and documents with a native GTK interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B open-media-converter
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ files ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open Media Converter converts video, audio, images and documents. Add files,
configure section settings or per-file presets, and start a conversion batch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show command-line usage.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Show the application version.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable diagnostic logging.
.TP
.BI --config-dir " directory"
Use an alternative configuration directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JAVA_HOME
Select a Java 23 or newer installation.
.TP
.B OMC_DEBUG
Set to 1 to enable diagnostic logging.
.TP
.B OMC_LOG_LEVEL
Select the console and file log level (INFO by default). Overrides OMC_DEBUG;
the --debug option takes precedence over either variable.
.TP
.B OMC_LOG_DIR
Use this exact directory for app.log, conversion.log and error.log.
LOG_DIR is accepted when OMC_LOG_DIR is unset.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for application logs; defaults to ~/.local/state.
Must be an absolute path.
.TP
.B GTK_THEME
Override the GTK theme.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/open-media-converter/
stores settings, presets and session state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/open-media-converter/logs/
stores logs unless XDG_STATE_HOME or a log directory override is set.
Logs rotate daily or at 2 MB into gzip archives, kept for seven days with
a 12 MB archive cap per log, in addition to each active log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pandoc (1),
.BR convert (1),
.BR libreoffice (1)
